                'description' => '<h3>Standalone 3-Axis DSP Motion Control Pendant</h3><p>The RichAuto A11 DSP system is an industrial standalone CNC handheld motion controller engineered to replace unstable PC-based control setups in high-vibration, high-dust workshop environments. Operating independently without requiring a dedicated computer tower or sensitive PCI breakout cards, the A11 communicates via an optically isolated 50-pin differential ribbon cable connected directly to the central machine interface board.</p><p>Equipped with high-performance 32-bit DSP processing architecture, the A11 executes standard ISO G-code and PLT vector files with smooth look-ahead S-curve velocity profiling. In continuous commercial operations, its standout safeguard is power-fail recovery: if mains electricity drops abruptly, the system immediately locks the exact XYZ toolpath coordinates into non-volatile flash memory, enabling operators to resume uninterrupted machining from the exact millisecond breakpoint once power returns. Built-in error alarm monitoring tracks spindle status and drive faults in real time, preventing tool crashes and scrapped workpieces.</p><h4>Operational & Engineering Highlights:</h4><ul><li>Complete PC-Free Operation: Eliminates Windows OS crashes, driver incompatibilities, virus corruption, and workshop dust ingress into computer fans.</li><li>Intelligent File Pre-Checking: Inspects uploaded G-code files prior to machining to catch syntax anomalies, out-of-bounds coordinates, and toolpath limits.</li><li>Real-Time Spindle & Drive Error Interlock: Instantly halts machine motion upon detecting driver fault signals or inverter trip alarms.</li><li>One-Key Origin & Return to Reference: Simple operator functions for mechanical homing, work coordinate zeroing, and auto tool-setter calibration.</li></ul>',
