                'slug' => 'yako-2608-stepper-drivers',
                'short_description' => 'Industrial 2-phase hybrid stepper driver delivering 6.0A peak current with DC 24V-110V / AC 18V-80V input. Features 16 selectable microstep subdivisions and 200Kpps pulse frequency for smooth low-noise axis motion.',
                'description' => '<h3>High-Performance 2-Phase Hybrid Stepper Drive</h3><p>The Yako YKD2608MH-Dk is an industrial-grade, constant-torque microstep driver purpose-built for driving high-torque NEMA 34 and NEMA 42 2-phase hybrid stepper motors on CNC machine axes. Operating over a versatile power supply range of DC 24V–110V or AC 18V–80V, it integrates specialized bipolar constant-current PWM chopping circuitry that actively suppresses low-speed motor resonance, vibration, and acoustic hum.</p><p>With 16 user-selectable microstep resolution settings ranging up to 256 subdivisions (51,200 pulses/rev), the 2608 series provides exceptionally fluid motion during intricate vector engraving while sustaining high holding torque during rapid gantry traverses. An automated 50% idle current reduction circuit activates within 100ms of pulse cessation, substantially minimizing motor heat buildup during dwell cycles. Optical isolation on all control inputs ensures dependable immunity against ground loops and industrial electrical noise.</p><h4>Engineering & Installation Guidance:</h4><ul><li>Heat Dissipation Design: Heavy-finned aluminum extrusion heatsink ensures passive cooling in well-ventilated cabinets.</li><li>DIP Switch Configuration: Easy 8-position switch sets current ratings from 2.0A to 6.0A and microstepping resolution on-the-fly.</li><li>Direct Mains Step-Down: Compatible with secondary winding of standard toroidal step-down transformers without DC rectifiers.</li><li>Fault Indication: Dual LED panel indicates power status (Green) and over-current/over-voltage trips (Red).</li></ul>',
