                'short_description' => 'Heavy-duty 5.5 kW water-cooled high-speed electrospindle operating at 24,000 RPM. Engineered with precision matched ceramic P4 angular contact bearings, ER25/ER32 collet chuck, and mirror-polished stainless body.',
                'description' => '<h3>Industrial 5.5 kW High-Speed Water-Cooled Spindle</h3><p>This genuine HQD 5.5 kW water-cooled electric spindle represents the industrial workhorse for demanding CNC machining centers, delivering consistent high-torque cutting performance across wood, dense MDF, stone, acrylic, and non-ferrous alloys. Built with a heavy cylindrical stainless steel housing (100mm outer diameter), the spindle incorporates an optimized internal water circulation jacket that efficiently draws heat away from the motor windings and bearing assemblies during round-the-clock production shifts.</p><p>Internally, the spindle is supported by 4 precision P4-grade angular contact ceramic bearings configured in a rigid back-to-back preloaded arrangement. This architecture guarantees microscopic spindle nose runout (<0.003 mm), completely suppressing tool deflection during heavy profile roughing and high-feed 3D surface finishing. The precision-balanced rotor minimizes harmonic vibration across its entire 6,000 to 24,000 RPM operational envelope, dramatically extending cutter life and ensuring glassy edge finishes.</p><h4>Technical & Cooling Best Practices:</h4><ul><li>Coolant Circulation: Requires continuous flow of clean water or water/glycol mix via industrial chiller (CW-5000 or submersible pump).</li><li>VFD Tuning: Must be operated through a matched 5.5kW or 7.5kW variable frequency inverter configured for 400Hz base frequency.</li><li>Collet Maintenance: Keep ER25/ER32 collet bore clean and free of resin buildup; torque collet nut to specified Newton-meter rating.</li><li>Thermal Protection: Embedded PTC thermistors safeguard motor stator against unintended overheating.</li></ul>',
