                'description' => '<h3>Heavy-Duty Semi-Open Cable Carrier Track (35 x 75 mm)</h3><p>The DR35 series cable drag chain (energy carrier track) is engineered to guide, support, and protect dynamic power lines, high-flex motor cables, encoder wiring, and pneumatic/coolant tubing on high-cycle CNC machinery. Fabricated from modified reinforced polyamide (Nylon PA66), this carrier provides exceptional tensile strength, impact toughness, and wear resistance even in workshops exposed to abrasive sawdust, oily lubricants, and plastic shavings.</p><p>Featuring a semi-open design with snap-open crossbars along both the inner and outer radii, the DR35 allows technicians to rapidly lay in or replace pre-terminated cables without disconnecting plugs or dismantling the entire axis. Reinforced stop dogs between individual chain links maintain a stable 50mm bending radius, preventing sharp cable kinks that cause internal conductor fatigue. Rotating end connector brackets with integrated strain relief allow flexible linear or circular mounting configurations.</p><h4>Engineering Highlights & Advantages:</h4><ul><li>Subsequent Cable Laying: The chain can be opened from both inside and outside curves, allowing pre-assembled cables with bulky plugs to drop in effortlessly.</li><li>High Structural Stability: Multiple large internal stops and large connecting pins ensure high force-absorption under rapid 2g gantry acceleration.</li><li>Simple Length Adjustment: Individual links can be added or removed in seconds using a flathead screwdriver while installed on the machine.</li><li>Metal-Insert Fastening: End connector mounting holes feature integrated metal reinforcement to eliminate plastic cold-flow and screw loosening.</li><li>Integrated Strain Relief: Mounting brackets incorporate tie-wrap combs to secure cables firmly, preventing push-pull tension on motor terminals.</li><li>100% Recyclable: Manufactured from premium non-toxic, recyclable engineering polyamide.</li></ul>'