                'slug' => '670mm-helical-rack',
                'short_description' => 'Precision Module 1.25 ground helical gear rack (670mm length) with induction-hardened teeth (HRC 45-50), pre-machined mounting bores, and black oxide anti-corrosion finish. Delivers high-load, low-backlash linear motion.',
                'description' => '<h3>Module 1.25 Precision Ground Helical Rack & Pinion Drive</h3><p>This 670mm precision helical rack (Module 1.25) is the core linear motion drive transmission component utilized on modern high-speed CNC routers, laser cutters, and automated gantry bridges. Unlike straight-tooth spur racks where contact occurs abruptly along the entire tooth width, helical racks engage gradually along an angled 19°31\'42" pitch line. This angular contact provides a dramatically higher tooth overlap ratio, distributing heavy gantry inertial forces across multiple meshing teeth simultaneously.</p><p>Manufactured from high-grade medium carbon steel (C45/SS) and finished with hot rolling, precision tooth grinding, and high-frequency induction hardening (HRC 45–50), this rack exhibits high resistance to pitting, surface wear, and tooth shear. Each 670mm section includes precision end-machined joint faces and standardized counterbored bolt holes, enabling seamless end-to-end butting along extended machine beds (e.g. 2500mm or 3000mm strokes) without pitch discontinuities or stepping jerks.</p><h4>Mounting & Alignment Guidelines:</h4><ul><li>Modular Splicing: Use a reverse companion rack section clamped across the joint seam to ensure perfect tooth pitch continuation before torquing mounting bolts.</li><li>Lubrication Protocol: Keep teeth lubricated with high-adhesion lithium grease or automated felt-gear pinion lubricator.</li><li>Backlash Adjustment: Mount reduction gearbox on an eccentric pivot or slotted plate to dial in 0.03mm-0.05mm running backlash.</li><li>Surface Hardening: Induction-hardened tooth flanks provide extended operational life under continuous heavy gantry reversing cycles.</li></ul>',
